 "coordinate_system": "Image coordinates of the source raster: pixel indices (0-based), x to the right, y downward, at raster resolution (1600 x 1050). Geometric measurements only; no coefficient or standard error is derived from them.",
 "measurement_method": "coverage level k = clip(B - R, 0, 139) of #2166AC over a neutral background; support S = {k >= 1}; hollow interiors = enclosed non-S regions >= 30 px; panel bounds and tick centres from the light grid lines (darkness-weighted centres); marker centre: y = midpoint of the rows whose k >= 70 span exceeds the 4 px bar width, x = k-weighted centroid of those rows. Re-measured and compared field by field by 04_restyle_wage_raster.py (read-only).",
 "ci_endpoint_choice": "02_render_figures.R draws each 95% bar between bar_core_rows_top_bottom: the first and last rows of the opaque bar core (k >= 70) outside the marker disk, i.e. the drawn interval endpoints. support_rows_top_bottom (k >= 1) additionally contains the 1-4 px anti-aliasing / resampling fringe, and core_rows_top_bottom_ci_endpoints also counts the marker disk, which at e = -1 (no bar; bar_core_rows_top_bottom = null) is only the marker footprint. Both are kept as provenance, not drawn.",
 "ci90_provenance": "Not measured; derived at render time. The historical producer (nested repo Vocational/5_Package, commit 96eec106c1d82821daaff2f0b8d0512d99d190fa, 11 August 2026, 1_Codes/3_Analysis/08_survey_outcomes.R, lines 447-458 and 511-517) estimated did::att_gt(bstrap = TRUE, biters = 1999, cband = FALSE), aggte(type = 'dynamic'), and drew ci_lower/ci_upper = att -/+ 1.96 * se, i.e. pointwise normal 95% bars. 02_render_figures.R therefore draws the 90% bar as centre + r * (95% endpoint - centre) with r = qnorm(0.95) / 1.96 = 0.83921103, from centre_xy and bar_core_rows_top_bottom. Graphical re-expression at raster resolution (~1 source px); no coefficient or SE is recovered.",
 "rendering": "02_render_figures.R, plot_single(): same ggplot template as the other three figures (11 x 7.5 in, 300 dpi, circle 21 size 2.0, 95% bar linewidth 0.4 and 90% bar linewidth 1.3, both #72B1D4). Axes in source pixel units with scale_y_reverse, limits = panel_bounds_px (expand 0), breaks = x/y_tick_centres_px with the original printed labels; zero line at y_tick_centres_px['0']; onset line at the weighted centroid of onset_line_cols_profile.",
 "historical_masks": "wage_geometry_support_mask.png (S x 255), wage_geometry_alpha.png (k), wage_geometry_hollow_mask.png (hollow interiors x 255) and wage_geometry_class_mask.png (marker/bar partition, encoding below) were written by the earlier recolouring script (retired 2026-11-02). They are kept as measurement records and are re-checked by 04_restyle_wage_raster.py; they are not used for rendering.",
